      "argument": [
        {
          "id": "S001",
          "text": "Fix x∈ℝ^n and t>0. H001 gives positive finite dimensions and H002 permits all derivatives used here. By H004, u·u=1. Differentiation in time, by the ordinary product rule for the finite component sum defining the dot product, gives 2u·u_t=0, hence u·u_t=0. Choose the pointwise scalar a from H005. Then u_t·(u_tt−Δ_xu)=a(u_t·u)=0. This uses no derivative or regularity of a.",
          "uses": [
            "H001",
            "H002",
            "H004",
            "H005"
          ],
          "uses_local": [],
          "objects": [
            "n",
            "m",
            "x",
            "t",
            "u",
            "u_t",
            "u_tt",
            "Δ_xu",
            "a"
          ],
          "produces": [
            {
              "id": "F001",
              "statement": "u(x,t)·u_t(x,t)=0 and u_t(x,t)·(u_tt(x,t)−Δ_xu(x,t))=0.",
              "objects": [
                "x",
                "t",
                "u",
                "u_t",
                "u_tt",
                "Δ_xu"
              ],
              "binders": [],
              "assumptions": []
            }
          ],
          "introduces": [],
          "discharges": []
        },
        {
          "id": "S002",
          "text": "Twice differentiating u·u=1 in time gives 2|u_t|²+2u·u_tt=0. For each coordinate j0=1,...,n, twice differentiating in x_j similarly gives 2|∂_{x_j0}u|²+2u·∂_{x_jx_j0}u=0. Thus u·u_tt=−|u_t|² and u·∂_{x_jx_j0}u=−|∂_{x_j0}u|². Dot the normality equation for a with u and use |u|²=1. Finite distributivity and the definition of Δ_xu give a=u·(u_tt−Δ_xu)=Σ_{j=1}^n|∂_{x_j0}u|²−|u_t|². The same calculation applies to every scalar satisfying that pointwise equation.",
          "uses": [
            "H002",
            "H004",
            "H005"
          ],
          "uses_local": [],
          "objects": [
            "n",
            "x",
            "t",
            "u",
            "u_t",
            "u_tt",
            "D_xu",
            "Δ_xu",
            "a",
            "j0"
          ],
          "produces": [
