                }
              ],
              "assumptions": []
            }
          ],
          "introduces": [],
          "discharges": []
        },
        {
          "id": "S003",
          "text": "F001 proves the two orthogonality identities at the arbitrary point. By F002 substitute the computed value of a into the pointwise normality equation from H005 to obtain u_tt−Δ_xu=(Σ_{j=1}^n|∂_{x_j}u|²−|u_t|²)u. The scalar was chosen only at this point and is eliminated; it is not promoted to a regular scalar field. Generalizing x and t proves all the asserted pointwise identities.",
